{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_EMnKO0xDVjOpkOj2CSNsG4rA","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-03 1x:xx +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (engineer round — P7-a)\n4\tWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p7a (branch feat/p7a-exec-budget @ origin/master)\n5\t\n6\t# Task: P7-a — the guest execution budget (your own ruled contract, from the stress ruling)\n7\t\n8\tYour earlier ruling (the PHPT stress-cost adjudication, collab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log in the main checkout) ruled the contract; this round implements it:\n9\t\n10\t- An OPTIONAL, per-run safepoint-count budget on the PHP execution profile. The test harness run-vm may pass it; production behavior is unchanged unless a composition explicitly supplies a budget (default unlimited/off).\n11\t- Count the EXISTING PHP :loop and :call safepoint hooks; no generic VM-instruction accounting.\n12\t- Exhaustion raises the documented PHP OPERATIONAL FATAL, using the pinned PHP text — not the JavaScript Interrupt exception. It is not guest-catchable and skips destructor shutdown (docs/design/yang.php.md:1239, :1921-1938, :2093-2097).\n13\t- No wall-clock timeouts as guest semantics; this bounds execution between hooks only.\n14\t- Document it in yang.php.md (a short P7-a subsection or an amendment to the safepoint section).\n15\t\n16\t## Gate\n17\t\n18\t1. New focused tests: a bounded run exhausts and raises exactly the pinned fatal on all four VMs; an unbounded run (no budget) behaves identically to today; a budget that is never exhausted is unobservable.\n19\t2. The php consumer namespaces stay green (class-model/objects/generators at minimum); cljstyle/kondo clean.\n20\t3. COMMIT on feat/p7a-exec-budget (feat(yang.php): the optional safepoint-count execution budget), no Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push. Findings to collab/orch-lane/1794260000000-engineer-p7a-budget.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md (uncommitted)."}
