{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_UqkA7tSo2BY3u1KZ78XO8WvL","content":"1\t(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n2\t yang.php.antlr.prelude-module\n3\t  \"The include/require runtime of the PHP profile (docs/design/yang.php.md\n4\t   section 11, plan P6 R3/R4): the four kinds, the `_once` check, the two\n5\t   missing stages. Guest code like the rest of the prelude; the lowering\n6\t   emits only applications of these names.\n7\t\n8\t   Runtime state `php/init!` allocates for it (prelude.cljc owns the keys):\n9\t     php.rt/included   a cell, map of normalized path to true; written on\n10\t                       `:ok` delivery only, never on a refusal\n11\t     php.rt/unit       a cell, the executing unit's path or :php/null\n12\t     php.rt/path-map   a cell, map of normalized path to a delivery thunk\n13\t                       (the literal path map of the composition's `:paths`)\"\n14\t  (:require\n15\t    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n16\t    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]))\n17\t\n18\t\n19\t(def include-path-text\n20\t  \"The `include_path` the missing-include texts print: the oracle image's\n21\t   default. PENDING the S0 oracle pin (php:8.3-cli reports\n22\t   `.:/usr/local/lib/php`).\"\n23\t  \".:/usr/local/lib/php\")\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(def include-kinds\n27\t  \"The four kinds the lowering passes to `php/include-run`.\"\n28\t  #{:include :include-once :require :require-once})\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(defquoted ^:private module-forms\n32\t  \"The include definitions, `[store-key form]`.\"\n33\t  '[[php/include-kind-name\n34\t     (fn [kind]\n35\t       (if (= kind :include)\n36\t         \"include\"\n37\t         (if (= kind :include-once)\n38\t           \"include_once\"\n39\t           (if (= kind :require) \"require\" \"require_once\"))))]\n40\t    [php/include-require?\n41\t     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :require) true (= kind :require-once)))]\n42\t    [php/include-once?\n43\t     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :include-once) true (= kind :require-once)))]\n44\t    [php/warn-refusal\n45\t     ;; php/warn with the structured refusal on the record (plan R4)\n46\t     (fn [errno msg refusal]\n47\t       (let [rec (assoc (php/warn-record errno msg) :yang.php/refusal refusal)\n48\t             h (cell/get php.rt/error-handler)]\n49\t         (if (= h :php/null)\n50\t           (php/warn-sink rec)\n51\t           (if (= (php/invoke-handler h errno msg) false)\n52\t             (php/warn-sink rec)\n53\t             :php/null))))]\n54\t    [php/include-missing!\n55\t     ;; the refusal map follows the base kind; the texts carry the kind as\n56\t     ;; written; a refused path is never marked included\n57\t     (fn [path kind refusal]\n58\t       (let [nm (php/include-kind-name kind)]\n59\t         (do (php/warn-refusal\n60\t               2\n61\t               (data/str-concat\n62\t                 (data/str-concat (data/str-concat nm \"(\") path)\n63\t                 \"): Failed to open stream: No such file or directory\")\n64\t               refusal)\n65\t             (if (php/include-require? kind)\n66\t               (php/throw-error\n67\t                 \"Error\"\n68\t                 (data/str-concat\n69\t                   (data/str-concat\n70\t                     (data/str-concat \"Failed opening required '\" path)\n71\t                     \"' (include_path='\")\n72\t                   (data/str-concat php/include-path \"')\")))\n73\t               (do (php/warn-refusal\n74\t                     2\n75\t                     (data/str-concat\n76\t                       (data/str-concat\n77\t                         (data/str-concat\n78\t                           (data/str-concat nm \"(): Failed opening '\")\n79\t                           path)\n80\t                         \"' for inclusion (include_path='\")\n81\t                       (data/str-concat php/include-path \"')\"))\n82\t                     refusal)\n83\t                   false)))))]\n84\t    [php/include-body\n85\t     ;; marks the path before the body runs, names the unit while it runs,\n86\t     ;; answers the body's `return` value, else 1\n87\t     (fn [path delivered scope ctx]\n88\t       (let [prev (cell/get php.rt/unit)]\n89\t         (do (cell/set! php.rt/included (assoc (cell/get php.rt/included) path true))\n90\t             (cell/set! php.rt/unit path)\n91\t             (php/try-finally\n92\t               (fn []\n93\t                 (let [v ((get delivered :body) scope ctx)]\n94\t                   (if (= v :php/no-return) 1 v)))\n95\t               (fn [x] (cell/set! php.rt/unit prev))))))]\n96\t    [php/include-run\n97\t     ;; `thunk` answers {:status :ok :body b} or the structured refusal\n98\t     (fn [path thunk kind scope ctx]\n99\t       (if (if (php/include-once? kind)\n100\t             (not (nil? (get (cell/get php.rt/included) path)))\n101\t             false)\n102\t         true\n103\t         (let [r (thunk)]\n104\t           (if (= (get r :status) :ok)\n105\t             (php/include-body path r scope ctx)\n106\t             (php/include-missing! path kind r)))))]\n107\t    [php/normalize-path\n108\t     ;; the computed arm's lookup key: leading \"./\" segments dropped\n109\t     (fn [s]\n110\t       (if (if (>= (data/str-length s) 2) (= (data/substring s 0 2) \"./\") false)\n111\t         (php/normalize-path (data/substring s 2))\n112\t         s))]\n113\t    [php/include-computed\n114\t     ;; a computed path is a run-time lookup in the published path map; a\n115\t     ;; miss is the run-time missing-include behaviour for the kind\n116\t     (fn [pathv kind scope ctx]\n117\t       (let [path (php/normalize-path (php/to-string pathv))\n118\t             thunk (get (cell/get php.rt/path-map) path)]\n119\t         (php/include-run\n120\t           path"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_05uMwXQdt0nz682Tazuw1Vur","content":"1\t(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n2\t yang.php.antlr.prelude\n3\t  \"The PHP runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n4\t   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3.5, 7, 9). PHP semantics for operators,\n5\t   juggling, comparison, output and errors live here as guest code, not in\n6\t   Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n7\t\n8\t   Value encoding (P1):\n9\t     int             host integer in [-2^63, 2^63-1] (a BigInt carrier on JS\n10\t                     past 2^53); every operator computes the exact result\n11\t                     through the `integer` module and demotes to float when\n12\t                     it leaves the range\n13\t     float           untagged Jing float64 content (`data/float64`), the\n14\t                     shared ruling of yang.typescript.md section 2; the kind\n15\t                     test is `php/kind`, never a second tag. The prelude\n16\t                     holds no integral float literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1):\n17\t                     floats are built with `data/float64` or computed, and\n18\t                     host arithmetic only ever sees `data/float-value`\n19\t     string          a host string whose every char is one byte (a latin-1\n20\t                     carrier); the lowering resolves literal text to bytes\n21\t     bool            host true / false\n22\t     null            :php/null\n23\t     array           {:php/type :array :index {key value} :order [key ...]\n24\t                     :next-index n}: a persistent ordered map; keys are\n25\t                     ints or strings (`php/array-key`); `:next-index` is\n26\t                     absent until the first integer key is written\n27\t     error object    {:php/type :obj :class name :ord n :props {\\\"message\\\"\n28\t                     \\\"code\\\" \\\"previous\\\"}}\n29\t     function        a cell {:php/type :function :name s :code (fn [args])\n30\t                             :yang.call/entry (fn [invocation])}\n31\t\n32\t   Runtime state is allocated by `php/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n33\t   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\n34\t   `:php/ready` as its last write):\n35\t     php.rt/ctx            the dynamic context {:handlers :depth :base :frame}\n36\t     php.rt/out            a cell holding the buffer stack, a vector of\n37\t                           buffers, each a vector of byte-string chunks;\n38\t                           `php/echo` conjs onto the last buffer, the\n39\t                           bottom buffer is never popped\n40\t     php.rt/globals        a cell holding the plain array of section 10.1\n41\t                           (`$GLOBALS`), `(php/empty-array)` initially\n42\t     php.rt/functions      a cell holding a map of lower-cased name to\n43\t                           function cell; builtins are pre-seeded\n44\t     php.rt/classes        a cell holding a map of class name to class record\n45\t                           (the Throwable hierarchy, data only)\n46\t     php.rt/next-ord       a cell, the per-task object ordinal\n47\t     php.rt/next-cell      a cell, the per-task counted-cell id (`:id`)\n48\t     php.rt/error-handler  a cell, :php/null or a callable\n49\t     php.rt/error-reporting a cell, the mask (E_ALL initially)\n50\t     php.rt/diag           a cell, the vector of diagnostic records\n51\t     php.rt/int-max, php.rt/int-min   exact integers computed in `init!`,\n52\t                           never literals (literals past 2^53 are not\n53\t                           portable)\n54\t\n55\t   Errors are raised with `php/raise`; with no handler frame above them they\n56\t   reach the unit root, `php/run-main`, which answers\n57\t   `{:php/out s :php/diag [...] :php/uncaught nil-or-{:class :message}}`.\n58\t\n59\t   Float text: `php/float-text x ndigit` is `zend_gcvt`; `ndigit` 14 is\n60\t   `echo` (precision), 17 is `var_dump` (serialize_precision -1, the\n61\t   shortest round trip from `integer/float-digits`).\n62\t\n63\t   Two emitters, one source: `definitions` is the only definition list.\n64\t   `uast` is the bundled prelude; `module-uast` is the same list as the\n65\t   linker module `php`. The module emitter strips only the module's own\n66\t   namespace `php/`; `php.rt/*` stays qualified.\n67\t\n68\t   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`.\"\n69\t  (:require\n70\t    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n71\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n72\t    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n73\t    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n74\t    [yang.core.call :as call]\n75\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n76\t    [yang.php.antlr.builtins :as builtins]\n77\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude-module :as module-defs]\n78\t    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]\n79\t    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t(def host-names\n83\t  \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n84\t  (into '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/nth data/subvec data/str-concat\n85\t           data/str-length data/str-join data/str-compare data/str->code-points\n86\t           data/code-points->str data/substring data/float64 data/float-value\n87\t           data/content= data/number? data/dissoc data/into\n88\t           integer/add integer/sub integer/neg integer/mul integer/compare\n89\t           integer/to-float integer/compare-float integer/true-div integer/pow\n90\t           integer/shift-left integer/shift-right integer/bit-and integer/bit-or\n91\t           integer/bit-xor integer/bit-not integer/from-float integer/quot-rem\n92\t           integer/floor-div-mod integer/format integer/parse\n93\t           integer/float-digits integer/decimal->float}\n94\t        call/host-names))\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n98\t  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n99\t  '[;; ----------------------