{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_amxwPQkbaIhcXgHBhtD85VAs","content":"docs/design/yang.php.md-1236-|    |                                    | without calling destructors. An    |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1237-|    |                                    | uncaught `Throwable` runs this     |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1238-|    |                                    | sequence after the error output;   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1239:|    |                                    | the VM's operational halts (budget |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1240-|    |                                    | exhaustion, cancellation) skip the |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1241-|    |                                    | destructor phase, as Zend skips it |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1242-|    |                                    | on fatal errors                    |\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1926-  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1927-- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1928-  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1929:  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1930-  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21).\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1931-- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1932-  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2092-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2093-| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2094-|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2095:|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2096:|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2097-|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2098-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2099-| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2317-| C21 memory and time | Engine: `memory_limit`,             | restricted; none |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2318-| limits              | `max_execution_time`,               | (operational)    |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2319-|                     | `memory_get_usage`. Here: the       |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2320:|                     | deterministic safepoint budget and  |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2321-|                     | no memory accounting;               |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2322-|                     | `memory_get_usage` returns a pinned |                  |\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2323-|                     | constant                            |                  |\n--\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2474-4. (B8.4) Warnings as diagnostic-stream records (recommended) versus a guest\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2475-   `Warning` exception class; the record model matches ADR 0004 and keeps `@`\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2476-   cheap.\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2477:5. (B8.5) The deterministic safepoint budget as the `max_execution_time`\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2478-   stand-in (recommended) versus refusing the ini.\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2479-6. (B8.6) Replace and delete the compiler frontend at P8 (recommended) versus\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2480-   keeping the compiler revision of `:yang/php` installed until a later date."}
