{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_eGVcwMeLfNXRTbu4k80imIiT","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.portable-harness\n2\t  \"What the JVM, Node and Dart lanes share: the host composition the PHP\n3\t   profile runs over, the `packet` helper that builds a CST packet from a\n4\t   nested form, and a parserless run of a packet on the AST walker.\"\n5\t  (:require\n6\t    [dao.stream :as stream]\n7\t    [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n8\t    [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n9\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n10\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n11\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n12\t    [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n13\t    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n14\t    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n15\t    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n16\t\n17\t\n18\t(def ^:private capability-secret \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n19\t\n20\t\n21\t(defn create-vm\n22\t  \"An AST walker composed with the harness's deterministic ring-buffer stream.\"\n23\t  ([] (create-vm {}))\n24\t  ([opts]\n25\t   (ast-walker/create-vm\n26\t     (merge {:make-stream\n27\t             (fn [capacity]\n28\t               (ringbuffer/create!\n29\t                 {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\n30\t                  ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n31\t             :capability-secret capability-secret}\n32\t            opts))))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t(defn- new-memory-log\n36\t  []\n37\t  (let [result (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})]\n38\t    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n39\t      (:dao.stream/handle result)\n40\t      (throw (ex-info \"PHP harness memory-log creation failed\" {:result result})))))\n41\t\n42\t\n43\t(defn- drain\n44\t  [handle]\n45\t  (let [start (get-in (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)\n46\t                      [:dao.stream/cursor])]\n47\t    (loop [cursor start, acc []]\n48\t      (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n49\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n50\t          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n51\t                 (conj acc (:dao.stream/value result)))\n52\t          acc)))))\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t(def integer-limits\n56\t  \"The `integer` limits the PHP compositions here install.\"\n57\t  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(def data-limits {::data/max-items 1048576})\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(defn host-registry\n64\t  \"The registry with the cell, data and integer modules installed, admitted\n65\t   by the PHP profile.\"\n66\t  []\n67\t  (-> (module/empty-registry)\n68\t      module/register-cell-module\n69\t      (data/register-data-module data-limits)\n70\t      (prelude/register-integer-module integer-limits)\n71\t      prelude/admit))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(defn linked-registry\n75\t  \"`host-registry` over the default registry, whose `require` handlers the\n76\t   linked profile needs.\"\n77\t  []\n78\t  (-> (module/default-registry)\n79\t      module/register-cell-module\n80\t      (data/register-data-module data-limits)\n81\t      (prelude/register-integer-module integer-limits)\n82\t      prelude/admit))\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t(defn packet\n86\t  \"A CST packet from a nested form: `[rule child ...]` for a rule (a keyword)\n87\t   and `[type text]` (type a string) for a token. Spans are zero-width: the\n88\t   lowering reads them only for diagnostics. Ids are preorder, as the parser\n89\t   numbers them, so generated names match a parsed packet's.\"\n90\t  [form]\n91\t  (let [out (volatile! [])]\n92\t    (letfn [(walk\n93\t              [f]\n94\t              (let [id (count @out)]\n95\t                (if (string? (first f))\n96\t                  (vswap! out conj {:id id, :kind :token, :type (first f),\n97\t                                    :text (second f), :span [0 0]})\n98\t                  (do (vswap! out conj nil)\n99\t                      (let [kids (mapv walk (rest f))]\n100\t                        (vswap! out assoc id {:id id, :kind :rule,\n101\t                                              :rule (name (first f)),\n102\t                                              :children kids, :span [0 0]}))))\n103\t                id))]\n104\t      (walk form))\n105\t    {:yang.cst/version 1,\n106\t     :yang.cst/unit [:hand 0],\n107\t     :yang.cst/grammar \"hand\",\n108\t     :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok,\n109\t     :yang.cst/root 0,\n110\t     :yang.cst/nodes @out,\n111\t     :yang.cst/complete true}))\n112\t\n113\t\n114\t(defn render\n115\t  \"The text a unit prints (ASCII here: the carrier is the text), then, for an\n116\t   uncaught error, the fatal line (no path).\"\n117\t  [{:php/keys [out uncaught]}]\n118\t  (str out\n119\t       (when uncaught\n120\t         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \" (:class uncaught) \": \" (:message uncaught)))))\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t(defn lower-through-stage\n124\t  \"`{:ast a :warnings w}` or `{:diagnostics d}` for `pk` through the lowering\n125\t   stage. Warning-severity diagnostics do not stop the program.\"\n126\t  [pk]\n127\t  (let [cst-log (new-memory-log)\n128\t        program (new-memory-log)\n129\t        diagnostics (new-memory-log)]\n130\t    (stream/append! cst-log pk)\n131\t    (lower/step-stage (lower/open-stage cst-log program diagnostics\n132\t                                        {:medium lower/program-medium}))\n133\t    (let [{warnings true, problems false}\n134\t          (group-by #(= :warning (:severity %)) (drain diagnostics))]\n135\t      (if (seq problems)\n136\t        {:diagnostics problems}\n137\t        (let [{:yin/keys [batch root]} (first (drain program))]\n138\t          {:ast (nth batch root), :warnings (vec warnings)})))))\n139\t\n140\t\n141\t(defn run-packet-raw\n142\t  \"The unit's value, `{:php/out :php/diag :php/uncaught}`, of packet `pk` on\n143\t   the AST walker, or `{:diagnostics d}`.\"\n144\t  [pk]\n145\t  (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (lower-through-stage pk)]\n146\t    (if diagnostics\n147\t      {:diagnostics diagnostics}\n148\t      (vm/value (vm/eval (create-vm {:modules (host-registry)}) ast)))))\n149\t\n150\t\n151\t(defn run-packet\n152\t  \"The rendered output of packet `pk` on the AST walker, or its diagnostics.\"\n153\t  [pk]\n154\t  (let [r (run-packet-raw pk)]\n155\t    (if (:diagnostics r) r (render r))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_D3743nVaHYF9Fx7GcAhpyBWp","content":"4880\t                              (php/msort (php/pairs arr 0 (php/array-count arr) []) cmp)\n4881\t                              keep))))]\n4882\t    [php/bi-sort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"sort\" args 1 false 1))]\n4883\t    [php/bi-rsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"rsort\" args 1 false -1))]\n4884\t    [php/bi-asort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"asort\" args 1 true 1))]\n4885\t    [php/bi-arsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"arsort\" args 1 true -1))]\n4886\t    [php/bi-ksort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"ksort\" args 0 true 1))]\n4887\t    [php/bi-krsort (fn [args] (php/do-sort \"krsort\" args 0 true -1))]\n4888\t    [php/bi-usort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \"usort\" args 1 false))]\n4889\t    [php/bi-uasort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \"uasort\" args 1 true))]\n4890\t    [php/bi-uksort (fn [args] (php/do-usort \"uksort\" args 0 true))]\n4891\t\n4892\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- unit\n4893\t    [php/bi-set-exception-handler\n4894\t     (fn [args]\n4895\t       (let [old (cell/get php.rt/exception-handler)]\n4896\t         (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handlers\n4897\t                        (php/vconj (cell/get php.rt/exception-handlers) old))\n4898\t             (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler (get args 0))\n4899\t             old)))]\n4900\t    [php/bi-restore-exception-handler\n4901\t     ;; back to the handler in force before the last `set_exception_handler`\n4902\t     (fn [args]\n4903\t       (let [stack (cell/get php.rt/exception-handlers)\n4904\t             n (data/count stack)]\n4905\t         (do (if (= n 0)\n4906\t               (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler :php/null)\n4907\t               (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler (get stack (- n 1)))\n4908\t                   (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handlers (php/args-prefix stack (- n 1) 0 []))))\n4909\t             true)))]\n4910\t    [php/handle-uncaught\n4911\t     ;; the user exception handler takes an uncaught throwable; the script then ends\n4912\t     (fn [exc]\n4913\t       (let [h (cell/get php.rt/exception-handler)]\n4914\t         (if (= exc :php/null)\n4915\t           exc\n4916\t           (if (= h :php/null)\n4917\t             exc\n4918\t             (do (cell/set! php.rt/exception-handler :php/null)\n4919\t                 (php/try (fn [] (do (php/call-value h (php/vconj [] exc)) :php/null))\n4920\t                          (fn [e] e)\n4921\t                          (fn [] :php/null)))))))]\n4922\t    [php/run-main\n4923\t     ;; the unit root: output, diagnostics and the uncaught error, if any\n4924\t     (fn [body]\n4925\t       (do (cell/set! php.rt/out [[]])\n4926\t           (cell/set! php.rt/ctx (php/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\n4927\t           (let [exc0 (php/try (fn [] (do (body) :php/null))\n4928\t                               (fn [e] e)\n4929\t                               (fn [] :php/null))\n4930\t                 exc1 (php/handle-uncaught exc0)\n4931\t                 exc2 (php/try (fn [] (do (php/shutdown!) :php/null))\n4932\t                               (fn [e] e)\n4933\t                               (fn [] :php/null))\n4934\t                 exc (if (= exc1 :php/null) exc2 exc1)]\n4935\t             (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :php/out\n4936\t                                  (data/str-join \"\" (get (cell/get php.rt/out) 0)))\n4937\t                           :php/diag (cell/get php.rt/diag))\n4938\t                    :php/uncaught\n4939\t                    (if (= exc :php/null) nil (php/snapshot-exc exc))))))]])\n4940\t\n4941\t\n4942\t(def ^:private builtins\n4943\t  \"The functions `php/init!` registers: PHP name to prelude definition,\n4944\t   derived from `builtins/supported`, the one table.\"\n4945\t  (mapv (fn [[nm {:keys [prelude]}]] [nm prelude]) (sort-by key builtins/supported)))\n4946\t\n4947\t\n4948\t(def builtin-names\n4949\t  \"The lower-cased names of the functions `php/init!` registers.\"\n4950\t  (set (map first builtins)))\n4951\t\n4952\t\n4953\t(def ^:private seed-classes\n4954\t  \"The builtin classes and interfaces `php/init!` seeds: [name kind parent\n4955\t   interfaces final?], parents before children (P4 owns the rest of the\n4956\t   builtin descriptor skeletons).\"\n4957\t  [[\"Traversable\" :interface nil []] [\"Iterator\" :interface nil [\"Traversable\"]]\n4958\t   [\"IteratorAggregate\" :interface nil [\"Traversable\"]] [\"ArrayAccess\" :interface nil []]\n4959\t   [\"Countable\" :interface nil []] [\"Stringable\" :interface nil []]\n4960\t   [\"JsonSerializable\" :interface nil []] [\"UnitEnum\" :interface nil []]\n4961\t   [\"BackedEnum\" :interface nil [\"UnitEnum\"]] [\"Throwable\" :interface nil [\"Stringable\"]]\n4962\t   [\"stdClass\" :class nil []] [\"Closure\" :class nil [] true]\n4963\t   [\"Generator\" :class nil [\"Iterator\"] true]\n4964\t   [\"Exception\" :class nil [\"Throwable\"]] [\"Error\" :class nil [\"Throwable\"]]\n4965\t   [\"ErrorException\" :class \"Exception\" []] [\"JsonException\" :class \"Exception\" []]\n4966\t   [\"RuntimeException\" :class \"Exception\" []] [\"LogicException\" :class \"Exception\" []]\n4967\t   [\"TypeError\" :class \"Error\" []] [\"ValueError\" :class \"Error\" []]\n4968\t   [\"ArithmeticError\" :class \"Error\" []] [\"DivisionByZeroError\" :class \"ArithmeticError\" []]\n4969\t   [\"ArgumentCountError\" :class \"TypeError\" []] [\"UnhandledMatchError\" :class \"Error\" []]\n4970\t   [\"InvalidArgumentException\" :class \"LogicException\" []]\n4971\t   [\"DomainException\" :class \"LogicException\" []] [\"LengthException\" :class \"LogicException\" []]\n4972\t   [\"OutOfRangeException\" :class \"LogicException\" []]\n4973\t   [\"BadFunctionCallException\" :class \"LogicException\" []]\n4974\t   [\"BadMethodCallException\" :class \"BadFunctionCallException\" []]\n4975\t   [\"OutOfBoundsException\" :class \"RuntimeException\" []]\n4976\t   [\"RangeException\" :class \"RuntimeException\" []]\n4977\t   [\"OverflowException\" :class \"RuntimeException\" []]\n4978\t   [\"UnderflowException\" :class \"RuntimeException\" []]\n4979\t   [\"UnexpectedValueException\" :class \"RuntimeException\" []]])\n4980\t\n4981\t\n4982\t(defn- throwable-members\n4983\t  \"The properties and native methods Exception and Error declare, which every\n4984\t   subclass inherits.\""}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_wJJsi6qntW2QDZeKputaGlHL","content":"1\t{\"role\":\"meta\",\"type\":\"system.version\",\"version\":\"2.4.0\"}\n2\t{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_94SiFvQKhbLiZQ5sRqfCe6Y8\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/tmp/orch/kimi-budget-ruling.md\\\"}\"}}]}\n3\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_94SiFvQKhbLiZQ5sRqfCe6Y8\",\"content\":\"1\\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-02 01:5x +0700\\n2\\tCoding-Agent: kimi\\n3\\tSession: fresh (read-only architect ruling)\\n4\\tMode: read-only\\n5\\t\\n6\\t# Ruling needed: the PHPT stress cost — guest execution budget or re-tiering?\\n7\\t\\n8\\tFollow-up to the P4 heap work. The engineer's fixture-by-fixture walk (collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md in worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4) found NO unbounded guest fixture. The recorded shiva \\\"hangs\\\" in yang.php.antlr.e2e-test (93 min at 100% CPU; thread dump collab/orch-lane/p4-e2e-hang-threaddump.txt in the main checkout, stack: run_loop <- vm_step <- test-utils/run-vm) and the PHPT selection (33+ min) are now best explained as finite stress cases that are simply expensive: Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt runs a fixed 10,001-iteration loop and takes ~259 s on one VM, and e2e-test carries phpt-derived stress cases; under two concurrent lanes on shiva the wall clock multiplies.\\n9\\t\\n10\\t## The question\\n11\\t\\n12\\tRule between the remedies:\\n13\\t\\n14\\t(a) A guest execution/step budget at the test-harness or engine-safepoint level (the engineer flagged this as architect territory — it may touch the safepoint contract in yang.php.md / yin.vm semantics). If you rule this way, define the smallest contract change: where the budget lives (run-vm test harness vs the engine's safepoint marks), what happens on exhaustion (interrupt? the existing Interrupt exception?), and whether production (non-test) semantics change at all.\\n15\\t\\n16\\t(b) Re-tiering: move phpt-derived stress cases (gc_013 and friends) behind the ^:slow tag (or DATOM_SLOW_TESTS) so the quick tier stays bounded, accepting the slow tier grows.\\n17\\t\\n18\\tOr both (a) for production robustness, (b) immediately for lane stability.\\n19\\t\\n20\\tAlso rule whether the 93-minute shiva e2e sighting is closed as \\\"finite stress cost, not a defect\\\" or must stay open until the remedy lands. Cite the safepoint docs you rely on. Read-only: do not edit.\"}\n4\t{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"I’ll check the fixture findings and the safepoint contract, then give a binding read-only ruling.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_yAW25Dn5JFc186g7Yv0aM55A\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md\\\"}\"}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_oXzmb1KRtS55AONVFYrBQHYe\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Grep\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"safepoint|step budget|Interrupt\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4\\\",\\\"glob\\\":\\\"*.md\\\",\\\"output_mode\\\":\\\"content\\\",\\\"-i\\\":true,\\\"head_limit\\\":200}\"}}]}\n5\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_yAW25Dn5JFc186g7Yv0aM55A\",\"content\":\"1\\t# P4 runaway guest investigation\\n2\\t\\n3\\t## Result\\n4\\t\\n5\\tNo unbounded guest loop was found in the e2e corpus available in this worktree. I did not add a guest step limit or alter corpus behavior: the remaining long case is a finite PHP-src stress fixture, and the PHP harness has no installed safepoint budget or host interrupt mechanism. A bound here would require a PHP safepoint integration or VM execution-budget semantics, so this is stopped for architect review per the task scope.\\n6\\t\\n7\\t## E2E fixture isolation\\n8\\t\\n9\\tRan each source through `e2e-harness/run-walker` in a daemon thread with a per-fixture timeout, covering base `programs/fixtures`, enabled P3b program fixtures (including the heap/reference cases), and enabled P4 program fixtures (including S8 generators). All completed with the 120-second ceiling; no fixture spun.\\n10\\t\\n11\\t- `sort-thousand` took roughly 90 seconds locally and exceeded the initial 30-second cutoff, then completed. Its source loop is bounded by `$i < 1000`.\\n12\\t- `gen-c8-pending-finally-departure` exceeded an initial 10-second all-VM cutoff, then completed in isolation: AST walker, semantic, stack, and register all returned `\\\"E\\\"`. This was a timeout that was too short, not a spin.\\n13\\t- The two selected PHPT sources containing literal `while (1)` also completed: `Zend/tests/bug44184.phpt` throws from the loop and is caught; `Zend/tests/bug66608.phpt` breaks from both loops.\\n14\\t\\n15\\tThe requested `collab/orch-lane/p4-e2e-hang-threaddump.txt` is absent in this worktree, so I could not compare the reported stack to this checkout's fixture IDs.\\n16\\t\\n17\\t## PHPT selection path\\n18\\t\\n19\\t`phpt_selection.edn` has 1,088 entries. The actual `phpt-selection-runs-test` did not finish under a 300-second wall-clock timeout. The largest selected finite loop I isolated was `Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt`: it runs `for ($i = 0; $i < 10001; $i++)`, took 258,911 ms through the walker, then reached an unsupported `gc_collect_cycles()` call. The similar `Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt` has two explicit finite bounds (9,999 and 10,001); the combined stress probe was still processing it when its 300-second wrapper expired. Other large loop cases found by source scan either have explicit numeric bounds or are marked `:needs :p4` and excluded from this selection.\\n20\\t\\n21\\tThese are finite stress cases, not loops that PHP itself would run forever. Reducing their iteration counts changes the GC threshold behavior under test. The harness currently runs guests directly via `run_vm` with no PHP step budget. The PHP design doc describes a future deterministic safepoint-count budget, but this worktree has no PHP safepoint hook/profile to install; shared `:line` support is also explicitly pending safepoint slice 3.\\n22\\t\\n23\\t## Architect decision needed\\n24\\t\\n25\\tPlease adjudicate the intended local quick-tier policy for the selected PHP-src GC stress cases and the mechanism for bounding guest execution. If the selected path needs an interruptible step budget, that requires the PHP safepoint contract/profile or engine execution semantics, outside this frontend fixture fix. No fixture was identified that can correctly be “bounded” at the source level without changing its meaning.\\n26\\t\\n27\\t## Verification\\n28\\t\\n29\\t- Fixture-by-fixture walker pass: completed; no timeout at the final 120-second ceiling.\\n30\\t- PHPT special `while (1)` candidates: both completed.\\n31\\t- `phpt-selection-runs-test`: did not complete within 300 seconds.\\n32\\t- No source/test files were changed; cljstyle/kondo were therefore not applicable.\"}\n6\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_oXzmb1KRtS55AONVFYrBQHYe\",\"content\":\"Tool output exceeded 50000 characters; the full output was saved to a file.\\ntool_name: Grep\\ntool_call_id: tool_oXzmb1KRtS55AONVFYrBQHYe\\noutput_size_chars: 55630\\noutput_size_bytes: 55818\\noutput_path: /Users/sto/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_datomworld-php-p4_b550d22cc7d2/session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05/agents/main/tool-results/Grep-tool_oXzmb1KRtS55AONVFYrBQHYe-2ab9537a-22a1-44db-ad27-0382ab4c144d.txt\\nnext_step: Use Read with output_path to page through the saved output, or Grep to search it.\\n\\n[preview: chars [0, 4096)]\\ncollab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:5:No unbounded guest loop was found in the e2e corpus available in this worktree. I did not add a guest step limit or alter corpus behavior: the remaining long case is a finite PHP-src stress fixture, and the PHP harness has no installed safepoint budget or host interrupt mechanism. A bound here would require a PHP safepoint integration or VM execution-budget semantics, so this is stopped for architect review per the task scope.\\ncollab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:21:These are finite stress cases, not loops that PHP itself would run forever. Reducing their iteration counts changes the GC threshold behavior under test. The harness currently runs guests directly via `run_vm` with no PHP step budget. The PHP design doc describes a future deterministic safepoint-count budget, but this worktree has no PHP safepoint hook/profile to install; shared `:line` support is also explicitly pending safepoint slice 3.\\ncollab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:25:Please adjudicate the intended local quick-tier policy for the selected PHP-src GC stress cases and the mechanism for bounding guest execution. If the selected path needs an interruptible step budget, that requires the PHP safepoint contract/profile or engine execution semantics, outside this frontend fixture fix. No fixture was identified that can correctly be “bounded” at the source level without changing its meaning.\\norchestrator-logs/1793292851-yang-python-retake.md:43:  (F1/F2 diagnosis, the Flutter pin, safepoint s4) stays recorded in known-gaps.md but is not this\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md:223:Done: (1) Slice-7 round 1 delivered by sonnet before expiry: guest library (all guest-side), apply intrinsic, TOTAL scaffold retirement, case_arms.edn + regeneration script, ledger closers. Local: focused 123/1265 -> after ANTLR gen 123/1273 green. (2) glm review (fresh session 0ae1fd6b after two failed stream-json/resume attempts — CLI quirks: stream-json needs --verbose in -p mode; a failed arg-parse run creates no session to resume): one P2 (library rem hangs on divisor 0 — infinite subtract-loop, no VM step budget) + 6 P3s, firsthand suite verification 85/768. (3) Gate allowance update committed 0c786d25: slice 7 REMOVED yang.clojure.cljc's host