:noninterruptible\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-506-   true}`, with `:runtime` the names of the runtime modules (default `py`,\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-507-   `pysp`) it passes through. `records` ({manifest [record-address ...]})\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-508-   are the local publication's records; a DHT source supplies none and the\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-509-   stage discovers them from the index datoms of its context. The stage\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-510-   reads only the context's `:store` and never fetches: it answers\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-511-   `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first address that store does\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-512-   not hold, and is run again once it is there. Answers\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-513-   `(fn [ctx name address])`: `{:status :ok :address address}` as published\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:514:   when noninterruptible, else the address of the instrumented module\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-515-   derived bottom-up from the verified sets (`:derivation` its `:derive`\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-516-   record's address), or the refusal naming the profile, the set and the\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-517-   `:name` refused.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-518-  [registry requirement records]\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-520-    (fn [ctx name address]\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-521-      (cond\\nResults truncated to 150 lines (total: 301). Use offset=150 to see more.\"}\n20\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_FS3fmFYjpvLALMVArCNpg8xF\",\"content\":\"test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-80-       (when uncaught\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-81-         (str \\\"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \\\" (:class uncaught) \\\": \\\" (:message uncaught)))))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-82-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-83-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:84:(defn run-vms\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-85-  \\\"`{vm-key rendered}` of `ast` on the four VMs; a host throw is\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-86-   `[:thrown message]`.\\\"\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-87-  [registry ast]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-88-  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :modules registry)\\n--\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-109-(defn run-php\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-110-  \\\"`{vm-key rendered}` for `source`, or `{:diagnostics d}`.\\\"\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-111-  [source]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-112-  (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (lower-program source)]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:113:    (if diagnostics {:diagnostics diagnostics} (run-vms (host-registry) ast))))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-114-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-115-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-116-(defn run-walker\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-117-  \\\"The ast-walker's rendering of `source` alone (fast iteration).\\\"\"}\n21\t{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_TGaek3O949ldhF2yefPAwUsL\",\"content\":\"No matches found\"}\n22\t{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"## Ruling: both, sequenced\\n\\n**(b) Re-tier immediately.** Keep ordinary PHPT cases in the quick tier, but move the curated PHPT stress cases—at minimum `gc_013`, `gc_023`, and their e2e-derived counterparts—behind `^:slow` / `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS`. Do not reduce iteration counts or otherwise alter fixture semantics. The current combined quick test is at `test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj:340`.\\n\\n**(a) Add the budget as a separate P7-a robustness change, not as a prerequisite for lane stability.**\\n\\nSmallest contract:\\n\\n- Add an **optional, per-run safepoint-count budget** to the PHP execution profile. `run-vm` may pass the option, but must not implement a host wall-clock timeout as guest semantics.\\n- Count the existing PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoint hooks; do not introduce generic VM-instruction accounting for this feature.\\n- Default is **unlimited/off**, so production behavior is unchanged unless a composition explicitly supplies a budget.\\n- Exhaustion is the documented **PHP operational fatal**, using the pinned PHP text—not the JavaScript `Interrupt` exception. It is not guest-catchable and skips destructor shutdown, consistent with `docs/design/yang.php.md:1239` and `docs/design/yang.php.md:1927`.\\n- This bounds guest execution between hooks; it is not a wall-clock guarantee around blocking host operations.\\n\\nThis follows the existing PHP contract: deterministic safepoint budget rather than nondeterministic `max_execution_time` (`docs/design/yang.php.md:1921-1938`, `docs/design/yang.php.md:2093-2097`). Generic engine step budgets remain an engine responsibility (`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:565-568`); safepoints are program stopping boundaries, not a license to change default execution semantics (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:655-659`).\\n\\n**Disposition of the 93-minute shiva sighting:** close the suspected **guest-nontermination defect now** as finite stress cost, supported by the fixture walk and measured `gc_013` completion (`collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:9-21`). Keep the **quick-tier lane-stability task** open until re-tiering lands; do not hold the hang investigation open for the budget work.\"}\n23\t{\"role\":\"meta\",\"type\":\"session.resume_hint\",\"session_id\":\"session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\",\"command\":\"kimi -r session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\",\"content\":\"To resume this session: kimi -r session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\"}"}
